closed_at":"2016-05-31T18:08:48Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"The changes in 717edaf5d399d2ffaf7b960ff3faa0606020b307 are a step in the right direction to provide a traceback-like message to git clone problems.  However, the message that gets appended at each level is always the original message, so you get stuff like this (newlines added for clarity):\n\n```\nERROR: /path/to/tensorflow/tensorboard/bower/BUILD:5:1:\nno such package '@paper_menu_button//':\nError cloning repository:\nhttps://github.com/polymerelements/paper-menu-button.git: cannot open git-upload-pack\ncaused by https://github.com/polymerelements/paper-menu-button.git: cannot open git-upload-pack\ncaused by https://github.com/polymerelements/paper-menu-button.git: cannot open git-upload-pack\ncaused by https://github.com/polymerelements/paper-menu-button.git: cannot open git-upload-pack\ncaused by https://github.com/polymerelements/paper-menu-button.git: cannot open git-upload-pack\nand referenced by '//tensorflow/tensorboard/bower:bower'.\n```\n\nIn the exception hander [here](https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/blob/2fba42e27ec517a8819236d15e45a42bfd5c1823/src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/bazel/repository/GitCloner.java#L177-L187) I think\n\n``` java\nerrmsg.append(\" caused by \" + e.getMessage());\n```\n\nshould be\n\n``` java\nerrmsg.append(\" caused by \" + throwable.getMessage());\n```\n\n(Is there a way to format a code diff in issues markdown?)\n","closed_by":{"login":"bazel-io","id":15028808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io","html_url":"https://github.com/bazel-io","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/followers","following_u